# Nintendo Game Boy Printer (gbprinter-libretro), retroXR's own core.
#
# Not an override: libretro has no such core, so this whole entry is ours and
# CoreInfoDatabase.load_overlay appends it.
#
# The core runs no CPU and loads no game. It joins the frontend's link bus on
# the "gb-sio-1" wire the retroXR builds of gambatte and mGBA speak, answers the
# Game Boy the way the MGB-007 does, and shows the paper as its video frame. Its
# two buttons are the printer's: A is FEED, B is TEAR (left stick X the number of
# lines to tear). Built from RetroXR/gbprinter-libretro, MIT.
#
# No systemid, on purpose. A systemid is a platform: a tile on the spawn menu and
# a roms folder, and a printer runs no games. It is offered where it belongs
# instead -- the printer on the Game Boy cards, its core on the Game Boy pages of
# OPTIONS > Cores > BIOS / Extras -- and GbPrinter starts it by name.

